//BUG="FEEDBACK.md 1.6 — an error at end of input carries the unknown position"
//ERR 23 4 23 7
//MSG="Unexpected token"

// TokenBlock::peek and ::get return LAST_TOKEN, whose position is
// FilePosition::unknown(), so an error raised when the parser runs out of
// tokens carries that sentinel instead of a real span. The compiler builds a
// perfectly good error and then display_error panics printing it:
//
//     Error: Unexpected token
//     thread 'main' panicked at src/display_error.rs:28:13:
//     internal error: entered unreachable code
//
// This case asks for the error to point at the incomplete assignment. The
// deeper problem is that there are two spellings of "no position" —
// Option::None and unknown() — and unknown() carries file_ident: 0, which is a
// valid file id, the user's own file. Collapse them, and make display_error
// degrade to message-only instead of panicking.
//
// The span below is this case's best guess at where the error belongs; adjust
// it to whatever the fix actually reports.

fn main
    x =
